-- title:
--   Scalarity of translation-equivariant endomorphisms of GL₃ principal series
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, write $\mathbb{Q}_v$ for the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\chi : \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \to \mathrm{Hom}(\mathbb{Q}_v^{\times}, \mathbb{C}^{\times})$ be a triple of characters which is injective as a function on $\mathrm{Fin}\,3$, i.e. the three characters are pairwise distinct. Let $\mathrm{principalSeries3}\ v\ \chi$ be the complex subspace of functions $f : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ that are locally constant, satisfy $f(u(x,y,z)g) = f(g)$ for all $x,y,z \in \mathbb{Q}_v$ and all $g$, where $u(x,y,z)$ is the upper triangular unipotent matrix with entries $x, y, z$, and satisfy $f(\mathrm{diag}(a_0,a_1,a_2)\,g) = \bigl(\prod_{i} \chi_i(a_i)\bigr)\cdot \bigl(\|a_0\|/\|a_2\|\bigr)\cdot f(g)$ for all $a \in (\mathbb{Q}_v^{\times})^3$ and all $g$. Let $T$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism of this space such that for every $g \in \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and every $f$ in the space, $T$ applied to the right translate $h \mapsto f(hg)$ of $f$ equals, as a function on $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$, the right translate $h \mapsto (Tf)(hg)$ of $T f$. Then there is $c \in \mathbb{C}$ with $T = c \cdot \mathrm{id}$.
--
--   This is the Schur-type statement that, for pairwise distinct inducing characters, the commutant of the right translation action on the normalised principal series of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ consists of scalars; no unitarity or irreducibility assumption is imposed. The proof rests on the bound [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.card_le_ncard_of_linearIndependent_of_upperUnipotent3_of_diagonal3`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.card_le_ncard_of_linearIndependent_of_upperUnipotent3_of_diagonal3), which limits the size of a linearly independent family of functionals transforming by a fixed character of the diagonal torus and invariant under the unipotent radical, and the result is in turn used in the analysis of cyclic subspaces generated by matrix coefficients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_exists_eq_smul_id_of_gl3AmbientRightTranslate_comm_of_injective.lean

